# Shell scripts keep Unix line endings on every machine.
#
# This repository is worked on from Windows with core.autocrlf on, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. For almost everything that is harmless. For a shell script it is fatal: bash
# reads the carriage return as part of each command and fails with "$'\r': command not found",
# on the first line, in a way that names nothing useful.
*.sh text eol=lf
